* START-HISTORY:
* 01 Oct 26 SD Core Solo - SOLO 25, ported from the multi-user product's
*           RELEASE_1.1 116.
* 01 Oct 26 SD Core Solo - USRDIR's backslashes are made @ds (which is "/")
*           before the separators are counted: BACKUP.ACCOUNT's first run
*           refused with 12041 because the count was always zero.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    call !acc_os_info(acc.name, acc.rec, info, err)
*
* A per-OS helper of BACKUP.ACCOUNT (see !acc_archive).  info is one manifest
* line per field, "key: value".
*
* SOLO HAS ONE ACCOUNT, sduser (ruling 29), and none of the multi-user
* product's per-account Windows state: no sdu_/sdg_ group, no sdssh/sdapi
* membership, no os.users.  So for an account this returns only:
*    type        USER, always
*    os.user     the Windows user this Solo runs as (env USERNAME)
* ssh and the API are on or off for the whole installation in Solo, not per
* account, so no route.* keys are written; SETTINGS.REPORT shows them.  (Agreed
* with SD Core for Linux, 2 Oct 2026: the shared reader accepts route.*,
* os.group and members ABSENT for a *-solo product and a Solo restore applies
* none of them.)
*
* WITH acc.name EMPTY, the system keys: product (windows-solo), host,
* accounts.root (the directory holding user_accounts - the parent of USRDIR,
* which follows the tree), sd.version, and restart - the command a user types
* to put a pending restore in place, shown verbatim in shared message 13035
* (agreed 2 Oct 2026).  sd -restart runs start_sd(), which applies the pending
* restore before SD starts (sysseg.c apply_pending_restore), and so does the
* startup task at boot.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine acc_os_info(acc.name, acc.rec, info, err)
$catalog !acc_os_info

   info = ''
   err  = ''

   if acc.name = '' then
      usr.dir = config('USRDIR')
*     01 Oct 26 - @DS IS "/" IN THIS PORT (gplsrc/sddefs.h, DS) AND USRDIR IS A
*     NATIVE WINDOWS PATH, C:\Users\...\user_accounts, WITH BACKSLASHES.  Counting
*     @ds in it as it stood always answered 0, so the owner's first BACKUP.ACCOUNT
*     stopped here with 12041 and the path it had just been handed.  Make it the
*     same separator the rest of the verbs build with (dest:@ds:name).
      usr.dir = convert('\', @ds, usr.dir)
      loop while usr.dir[len(usr.dir), 1] = @ds and len(usr.dir) > 3
         usr.dir = usr.dir[1, len(usr.dir) - 1]
      repeat
      n = count(usr.dir, @ds)
      if usr.dir = '' or n = 0 then
         err = 12041 : @vm : 'USRDIR' : @vm : usr.dir
         return
      end
      info<1> = 'product: windows-solo'
      info<2> = 'host: ' : downcase(field(@hostname, '.', 1))
      info<3> = 'accounts.root: ' : usr.dir[1, index(usr.dir, @ds, n) - 1]
      info<4> = 'sd.version: ' : system(1012)
      info<5> = 'restart: sd -restart, or restart Windows'
      return
   end

   info<1> = 'type: USER'
   info<2> = 'os.user: ' : env('USERNAME')
   return
end
